# Transflo @VERSION@

## What's new in 1.0.1
- Recipes and watch folders, plus Shortcuts, Spotlight and Siri actions.
- On-device text extraction, image descriptions, Smart Rename and 2× upscaling.
- ICO/ICNS icons, GIF compression, clipboard conversion and promised-file drops.
- Faster media encoding, improved trim sliders, favorites and batch progress.
- Compact Tools groups with hover/click navigation and Back, keeping every feature without repeated petals.
- Archive replaces Float on the Actions wheel; save selected files and folders into one ZIP.
- Recipes remain discoverable when the first conversion matches the input format, and stale hidden entries no longer hide saved recipes.
- A one-second Back hover and return pause prevent accidental group changes; saved Recipes have their own entry.
- Smaller wheels, icons and text for a lighter menu.
- Simpler General settings: Best, Balanced or Smaller; the Formats tab and saved size/percentage defaults are removed.
- Extract ZIP, RAR, TAR and GZIP archives into a new folder without overwriting existing files.
- Safer Undo and Shortcuts filenames; complete PDF OCR; reliable recipe cancellation,
  partial results, watch-folder ownership and multi-file promised drops.

Free, open-source file conversion at your cursor. Drag a file, tap a key, drop it on the wheel.

## Install
- **Homebrew:** `brew install --cask ali-fayed/transflo/transflo`
- **DMG:** download `Transflo-@VERSION@-arm64.dmg` below, open it and drag Transflo to Applications.
@FIRST_LAUNCH@
## What's inside
- **⇧ Convert:** 288 conversion paths across images, icons, audio, video, documents, PDF, slides, spreadsheets, subtitles and archives.
- **⌘ Tools:** 31 tools, from compress, crop and annotate to trim, bleep, merge, page editing, metadata, batch rename, text extraction, upscaling and Smart Rename, plus your own Recipes.
- **⌃ Actions:** AirDrop, Archive to ZIP, Copy, Move, Copy Path and Terminal.
- **Keyboard:** ⌥⌘Return on a Finder selection, plus Open in Transflo in the right-click menu.
- **Settings:** General (language, appearance, accent, keys, haptics, tick sound, preset compression and output naming), Wheel (size and what each wheel shows), Recipes (chained steps and watch folders), Compatibility (every conversion at a glance) and About (version and updates).
- **Editors:** focused editors for crop, rotate, adjust, annotate, redact, add or remove a background, collage, compress, trim, speed, split, merge, PDF pages, metadata and rename, with live previews and playback for audio and video.
- **Output defaults:** Best, Balanced or Smaller compression and output filename styles.
- **Getting Started:** a five-page tour with the current grouped wheel and selection style, replayable from the menu bar.
- **Updates:** a daily check that notifies you when a new version is out (switch it off in Settings › About), plus Check for Updates… in the menu. Update with the new DMG or `brew upgrade --cask transflo`.
- **Everything else:** a Jobs window, English and Arabic, light and dark, and VoiceOver support.

Requires macOS 14 or later on Apple silicon. File processing runs on your Mac. AirDrop shares files on request. The update check asks GitHub for the latest version number once a day and when you choose Check for Updates; nothing about you or your files is sent.

